cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Multicenter cardiac autonomic complexity in Parkinson's disease — analysis code and derived data"
abstract: >-
  Code and derived data for a multicenter study of cardiac autonomic complexity
  in Parkinson's disease, combining short resting ECG (CETRAM, Santiago),
  photoplethysmography during resting-state fMRI (Hospital Universitario Cruces,
  Bilbao) and 24-hour ambulatory Holter ECG (Nagoya University Hospital).
  Complexity is quantified by refined composite multiscale entropy (rcMSE) with a
  fixed tolerance, computed in Julia; all downstream statistics and figures are
  in Python.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/leonelmd/Multicenter_HRV_Complexity"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-25"
keywords:
  - Parkinson's disease
  - heart rate variability
  - multiscale entropy
  - cardiac autonomic dysfunction
  - refined composite multiscale entropy
  - biomarker
